  "upload": {
    "title": "This SUV Drove Into a Lake… and Floated 🌊 #shorts",
    "description": "A $150,000 SUV that can float. 🌊\n\nBYD's Yangwang U8 has an emergency floating mode. When the water gets too deep, the engine shuts off, the windows seal, the A/C switches to recirculation, the suspension rises to its maximum height and the sunroof opens as an escape hatch. It can stay afloat for about 30 minutes and paddle forward at around 3 km/h just by spinning its wheels, thanks to four independent electric motors, one per wheel. The same setup lets it spin 360 degrees in place like a tank. And it weighs almost 3.5 tons (about 3,460 kg).\n\nPrice: about 1.09 million yuan (~$150,000).\n\nWould you drive it into a lake? 👇\n\nSubscribe to Top Techs for more mind-blowing tech in under a minute.",
